{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he slept and dreamed a second time.</b> It does not say 'and he dreamed again' but rather 'a second time,' to indicate that it was one dream that was repeated twice. 'And behold, seven ears of grain growing on one stalk' (Genesis 41:5). And regarding the lean ones it does not say 'on one stalk,' because the seven years of plenty were consecutive, one after the other; therefore they grew on one stalk that bound them together. But the seven years of famine were not consecutive, for after two years of days, when Jacob came, the famine ceased and returned upon his death; therefore it does not say 'on one stalk.' And further, this indicates an abundance of produce, that even a single stalk would sprout seven ears, and good ones — a twofold measure of goodness. And the lean ones had a twofold measure of badness: that they grew one by one, and moreover they were blasted by the east wind. 'And Pharaoh awoke, and behold, it was a dream' (Genesis 41:7) — for he too understood that it was one dream."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:49.885052594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}